course: dictionary
lesson: 4373
title: Gypsum: a soft mineral
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Gypsum is a mineral, a natural solid found in rocks. It is usually white or grey. Read the words around it for clues. «The Cave of Crystals in Naica, Mexico, holds gypsum crystals up to about 12 metres long.» Crystals that long must have grown very slowly, over a very long time.
explain: The lessons say gypsum is soft: on the Mohs hardness scale it is 2, so your fingernail can scratch it. Try your meaning in a sentence. A soft mineral is easy to scratch, and that fits what we know about it.
explain: Gypsum is useful. It is used to make plaster, the chalk-like boards on walls called plasterboard, and plaster of Paris for casts. Some fertilisers contain it too. When you are unsure of a word, check the dictionary.
fact: Gypsum is a soft white or grey mineral found in rocks.
fact: Plasterboard, which covers many walls, is made from gypsum.
fact: Plaster of Paris, used for casts, is made from gypsum.
fact: On the Mohs hardness scale gypsum is 2, so you can scratch it with your fingernail.
fact: Gypsum forms when salty water dries up.
exercise: «The Cave of Crystals in Naica, Mexico, holds gypsum crystals up to about 12 metres long.» What is gypsum in this sentence? | A type of fish | A metal used in cars | *A mineral that forms crystals | A kind of warm water
exercise: Why can you scratch gypsum with your fingernail? | *It is soft, with a hardness of 2 on the Mohs scale | It is made of metal | It is wet and sticky | It is very hot
exercise: Which product is made from gypsum? | Steel pans | *Plasterboard for walls | Car tyres | Glass bottles
test: «The Cave of Crystals in Naica, Mexico, holds gypsum crystals up to about 12 metres long.» According to the sentence, what did the crystals grow in? | *Warm mineral water | Frozen ice | Cold sea water | Dry sand
test: Gypsum forms when what happens? | Rain falls on rocks | Snow melts | *Salty water dries up | Salty water boils over
exam: Which place has white sand made of gypsum? | Sahara Desert, Africa | *White Sands in New Mexico, USA | Death Valley, USA | Dead Sea, Jordan
